            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "oem/nvidia/bootstrap-credentials-oem-cmds.cpp",
                    "line": 88,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "rather than parsing through the channel file like this, it's probably better to use the channel_layer library that can do this for you:\n\n```\nconstexpr auto redfishHostInterfaceChannel = \"usb0\";\n// find the channel by name:\nint chNum = ipmi::getChannelByName(redfishHostInterfaceChannel);\nif (chNum < 0)\n{\n   return responseSensorInvalid();\n}\nChannelInfo chInfo{};\nif (ipmi::isValidChannel(chNum) != ipmi::ccSuccess || \n    ipmi::getChannelInfo(chNum, chInfo) != ipmi::ccSuccess)\n{\n    return responseSensorInvalid();\n}\n// check the mediumType, protocolType, isIpmi, sessionSupported\n...\nreturn responseSuccess(chNum);\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/nvidia/bootstrap-credentials-oem-cmds.cpp",
                    "line": 88,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/nvidia/bootstrap-credentials-oem-cmds.cpp",
                    "line": 161,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "It seems like we could choose a more appropriate response here. Maybe responseSensorInvalid() (0xCB) \"Requested Sensor, data, or record not present.\" or possibly an OEM response in the range of 0x01-0x7e specific for this command."
                },
